@# Compiler example; runtime story integration will use this later.

:: robin.study.peek [event robin study]
@heading "Robin's room"
@choices "What do you do?"

Tired of studying, you're unable to resist stealing a glance at Robin.
{{npc.robin.dependent|cap}} gaze is fixed on the textbook, lost in thought.

@if story.robin.hurt >= 1
Robin notices you looking and frowns.
@elseif npc.robin.relationship >= 0.5
Robin catches your eye and smiles.
@else
Robin remains focused on the textbook.
@endif

@choice study "Study" -> robin.study.back
  @icon 📚
  @time 1h
@endchoice

@choice mess "Mess with Robin" -> robin.study.mess
  @icon 😈
  @when npc.robin.present
  @require player.energy >= 10 "You are too tired."
  @warning "This may annoy Robin."
  @preview relationship -0.02 "-Relationship"
  @effect relationship robin -0.02
@endchoice

@choice leave "Leave" -> @exit
  @icon 🚪
@endchoice

:: robin.study.back [event robin study]
@heading "Robin's room"

@onenter
  @effect set story.daily.robinStudyCompany true
@endonenter

You return your attention to the textbook.

@choice continue "Continue studying" -> robin.study.peek
  @time 1h
@endchoice

@choice leave "Leave" -> @exit
@endchoice

:: robin.study.mess [event robin study]
@heading "Robin's room"

You reach across the desk and interrupt Robin's careful notes.

@choice apologise "Apologise" -> robin.study.peek
  @effect relationship robin 0.02
@endchoice

@choice leave "Leave" -> @exit
@endchoice
